{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1203162-so-how-s-going","id":1203162,"title":"So...How's going?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-04T15:40:48-07:00","id":1203162,"title":"So...How's going?","content":"Did you already start playing? how's going?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:38:56-07:00","id":1203394,"title":"","content":"I've done a few pick-up games (the 1e adventure Wolfsheim and some follow-on about a cabal of evil snake-Scions collecting artifacts). My table has been really enjoying Scion. We didn't play 1st edition, but we all love the setting and the variant of the Story* rules that Scion uses. My players (using original characters) kind of prefer to play at a more &quot;action hero with enhancement&quot; level, rather than focusing on their big supernatural abilities, but we've had a couple of wonders used at appropriate moments. I've found that they definitely could have busted out with Purviews more often, but are kind of holding back.<br /> <br /> These are all warm-ups to my big thing, an urban fantasy/ tian xia mix set in Hong Kong. The players have already given me character concepts and a campaign framework, but we're waiting on character creation until my CtL mini-chronicle is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:47:33-07:00","id":1204741,"title":"","content":"I mastered my first Scion Origin last week.<br /> It was a one player/one storyteller game and my friend play an mexican archeologist (with Lara Croft influence) who don't know (yet) she's the daughter of quetzalcoatl.<br /> <br /> It was full of action, with some investigation to find a Tezcatlipoca ritual mask before it was used to free a Tzitzimime (a titanspawn) jailed in one of the smoking mirror hidden temple.<br /> <br /> If you speak french, you can find a report of the game here: <a href=\"https://www.casusno.fr/viewtopic.php?f=32&amp;t=32431\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.casusno.fr/viewtopic.php?f=32&amp;t=32431</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23715-poulpy","name":"Poulpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}